# Cloudflare redirects
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
#
# Calculia is a fully static site with no API: activity data ships in
# `tools/<slug>/data.js`, strings in `tools/<slug>/strings.*.js`, the
# shared core lives in `assets/js/`, and everything else is HTML/CSS.
# The site uses a plain folder layout (no client-side router), so the
# only redirect we actually need is a fallback so a stale path
# doesn't end up on Cloudflare's default JSON error. Cloudflare
# redirects only support redirect codes (301/302/303/307/308) and
# proxying (200); it cannot issue a raw `status: 404`, so we route
# the unknown path back to the landing page.
#
# NOTE: the canonical 404 handling is configured in `wrangler.toml`
# via `not_found_handling = "404-page"` (the Workers + static assets
# path serves `404.html` for any unmatched path). This `_redirects`
# rule covers the legacy Pages path if the project is ever flipped
# back to classic Pages and the worker-builds path is bypassed.
/*  /site/index.html  302